Patch 0014 (ported to upstream c3436be): adds `open var disableLigatures: Bool` to
TerminalView, suppressing OpenType ligatures in both renderers via cache-keyed attribute
injection. Wired via AppConfig.ligatures -> TerminalPane.applyLigatures(_:).

Port notes for c3436be:
- ShaperKey gained `fallbackTag: UInt64`; disableLigatures is added alongside it.
- shape() call site in buildShapedSegments reads terminalView.disableLigatures and passes
  it through. The shape() signature adds disableLigatures parameter after fallbackTag.
- MacTerminalView backing Bool, AppleTerminalView open property + getAttributes injection:
  unchanged from v1.15.0 port; context lines adjusted for upstream rewrite.

Re-ported to c86e1d8 (77 commits ahead of c3436be):
- FrameViewState gained enableOsc8Hyperlinks, useBrightColors, translucentCellBackgrounds,
  collapseBrightColorsToBase fields between glyphFallbackProvider and the closing brace.
  disableLigatures is added after glyphFallbackProvider in both struct and init.
- SnapshotRenderContext gained enableOsc8Hyperlinks, useBrightColors fields before
  collapseBrightColorsToBase. disableLigatures is added after useBrightColors.
  identity hasher combines disableLigatures after translucentCellBackgroundAlpha.
- ExternalRenderOwner.swift (new file) adds a FrameViewState.init(renderView:) extension;
  it must also assign disableLigatures = false (TerminalRenderView has no such property).
- MetalTerminalRenderer.swift: fallbackTag call site at line 2889, ShaperKey struct
  at 3586, shape() func at 3630, attributedString construction at 3646.

